      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "For a^(m/n), the denominator tells the root and the numerator tells the power.\n\n27^(2/3) = (∛27)^2 = 3^2 = 9.\n\nYou can also power first and root later when it stays simple.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
